    {
      "id": "reader-artifact",
      "layer": "reader",
      "summary": "Reader intent, composition, writer projection, actual-byte map/audit, review and closure.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Preserve requested intent, composition order, editorial dispositions and writer projection; surface an open material choice before route identity or planning checks. Resolve exact unique quote bindings on every run and expose a read-only plan/text view.",
        "Bind actual artifact bytes and spans to shared contracts, deterministic audit and route review. Review every body/note limitation and prohibited overclaim with current quoted evidence; audit optional forbidden regexes and report declared bindings.",
        "Derive passed or needs_repair from current reader/route quality and record judge_kind; only independent_context with distinct IDs allows a broad claim. Self-review keeps explicit risk. Edits stale closure; automatic v2 closure covers text/markdown only.",
        "Reader-chain commands take upstream records as file paths and compute the fingerprints and references a caller leaves out (fill_brief_fingerprints, fill_check_fingerprints, fill_closure_fingerprints); values the caller gives are still checked. Derive only absent visible content/limitation placements and shared fiction-unit fields once at the brief-request boundary before fingerprints; retain explicit values and name unplaced ids requiring an explicit disposition.",
        "Name the resolved absolute path when an artifact file cannot be read.",
        "Project the optional fiction voice_contract into writer input, leaving a missing payload as a gap and binding changes in the route and brief fingerprints.",
        "Before filling any fingerprint, name vanished units across every contract binding and route-review evidence reference without guessing replacement bindings. Document and smoke-check installable route examples and their finite bad-text catalog. Closure copies saved provider statuses; missing or failing required reports forbid broad claims and are named in residual risk.",
        "Own mode-aware revision provenance: derive real source bytes/units from the source manifest helper, check current target ids and canonical fingerprints, and supply a deterministic not-applicable record for new writing.",
        "Expose the same text block classification to route validators, including Chinese prose and list markers. Briefs optionally import missing native SourceGuard YAML anchors; handwritten rows take priority."
      ],
